  "worked_solution": "First, note that the function takes the form $y=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(Bx)$ with $B=3.$ \n\nThe horizontal scaling factor is given by \n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{B}=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nSo, the period is\n\n$$\n2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{B}=2\\pi \\cdot \\frac{1}{3}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\n$$\n\nWe can verify this in the graph shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14254788/assets/1c2acadc66515bf90d080e7ecf918dd48b73de66a3be89544f009396f93af562.png)",
